conventionally write as $\bexists{x < t}{!A(x)}$.
%
A \emph{bounded universal !!{formula}} is one of the form
$\lforall[x][(x < t \lif !A(x))]$ where $t$ is any term, which we
conventionally write as $\bforall{x < t}{!A(x)}$.
\end{defn}

