\begin{defn}
\ollabel{thm:oconsis-q}
A theory $\Th{T}$ is \emph{$\omega$-consistent} if the following holds: if
$\lexists[x][!A(x)]$ is any sentence and $\Th{T}$ !!{derive}s $\lnot
!A(\num 0)$, $\lnot !A(\num 1)$, $\lnot !A(\num 2)$, \dots then $\Th{T}$
