source_text:
\begin{proof}
Fix $s \in \onesphere$; there is some $r \in C$ such that $r \in
\equivrep{s}{\sim}$, i.e., $r \sim s$, i.e., $\rho(r) = s$ for some
$\rho \in \rotationsgroup$. 
\end{proof}

target_text:
\begin{proof}
$s \in \onesphere$ નિશ્ચિત લો;
કોઈ $r \in C$ એવું છે કે
$r \in \equivrep{s}{\sim}$,
એટલે $r \sim s$, એટલે કોઈ
$\rho \in \rotationsgroup$ માટે
$\rho(r) = s$.
\end{proof}

